  "reasoning": "The retrosynthesis involves disconnecting the biaryl bond in methyl 4-amino-3-(4-chlorophenyl)benzoate. This disconnection suggests a Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction between an aryl halide and an aryl boronic acid. The benzoate fragment requires a leaving group at the position ortho to the ester and meta to the amine, which corresponds to the bromine atom in methyl 4-amino-3-bromobenzoate. The chlorophenyl fragment is provided by 4-chlorophenylboronic acid. These two precursors are compatible with standard Suzuki coupling conditions.",
  "final_answer": "**Proposed Precursors:**\n1. **Methyl 4-amino-3-bromobenzoate**: `COC(=O)c1cc(Br)ccc1N` - provides the benzoate core with a bromine leaving group at the coupling site\n2. **4-Chlorophenylboronic acid**: `B(O)Oc1ccc(Cl)cc1` - provides the chlorophenyl fragment with the boronic acid coupling partner"
